A B S T R A C T
While dimethylammonium iodide (DMAI) is commonly utilized in inorganic CsPbI3 perovskite solar cells (PSCs), 
the protonation of DMA+ and the resulting degradation of precursors remain overlooked. Here, methyl­
ammonium formate (MAFa) is designed to inhibit organic cation deprotonation. Results show MAFa not only 
stabilizes DMA+ but also suppresses iodide ions (I−) oxidation to iodine (Io), yielding perovskite films with 
enhanced crystallinity and reduced defects. Additionally, a novel perfluorinated compound is introduced to 
passivate iodine vacancies (VI) —the dominant surface defects in CsPbI2.87Br0.13 films. These dual strategies 
synergistically boost the performance of n-i-p CsPbI2.87Br0.13 PSCs, achieving a power conversion efficiency 
(PCE) of 19.73 %. Remarkably, the devices retain 82 % of their initial PCE after 1,440 h under low humidity, far 
exceeding control counterparts.
