Manganese ion doped CsPbX3 perovskite quantum dots (QDs)
demonstrate high absorption of ultraviolet (UV) light and eﬃcient
orange emission with a large Stokes shift, and are almost transpar-
ent to visible light, which are ideal photon energy converters for
solar cells. In this work, Mn2+ ion doped CsPbCl3 QDs were syn-
thesized
by
incorporating
a
long-chain
ammonium
ligand
dodecyl dimethylammonium chloride (DDAC), in which the
DDAC ligand not only played the role of replacing the surface
ligands of QDs, but also enhanced the eﬃciency and stability of
Mn2+ ion doped QDs. The as-prepared QD sample displayed a
photoluminescence quantum yield (PLQY) as high as 91% and
served as a photon energy converter for silicon solar cells (SSCs).
The photoelectric conversion eﬃciency (PCE) of SSCs increased
from 19.64% to 20.65% with a relative enhancement of 5.14%.
This work displays a method to tune the eﬃciency of QDs by
modifying the surface ligands and an eﬃcient photon energy
converter for SSCs, which is of great importance for practical
applications.
