Luminescent solar concentrator-photovoltaic systems (LSC-PV) harvest solar light by using transparent
photoluminescent plates, which is expected to be particularly useful for building-integrated PV appli-
cations. LSC panels that absorb multiple wavelength bands are required to achieve high power conversion
eﬃciency (PCE). In this study, we demonstrate a pair of downshift LSC and photon upconversion (UC)
LSC, absorbing triple bands (violet, green, and red light). The UC is obtained by energy transfer and
triplet–triplet annihilation between sensitizer and emitter dyes. In particular, we exploit the dual sensitizer
to obtain absorption of the dual wavelength band. The couple with the UC LSC obtains photo-
luminescence of a single visible wavelength band from the LSC, which enables the use of wide bandgap
solar cells to absorb it. Here, we apply mixed-cation perovskite solar cells (PSCs) with high absorption
coeﬃcients, especially at visible wavelengths. In our triple-band-absorbing LSC-PSC, we achieve a
maximum PCE of 8.99%.
