                    deficits. However, understanding the mechanisms underlying the differences in passivation effects among various types of molecules remains limited, which is crucial for developing universal interface passivation strategies and guiding the design of passivation molecules. This study compares the passivation effects of phenethylammonium iodide (PEAI) and piperazine iodine (PI) on
                    <jats:italic>V</jats:italic>
