A R T I C L E I N F O  
Keywords: 
Perovskite solar cell 
Loss mechanism 
Nonradiative recombination 
Solar cell performance 
Power conversion efficiency 
A B S T R A C T  
With the progress in device research, the power conversion efficiency (PCE) of perovskite solar cells is contin­
uously improving and is approaching its theoretical limit. Nonetheless, it is still below the efficiency limit pre­
dicted by Shockley-Queisser owing to the presence of loss mechanisms. In this paper, we comprehensively 
analyze the loss factors limiting performance of devices utilizing an equivalent circuit model and identify the 
dominant loss mechanisms. The results demonstrate that Shockley-Read-Hall recombination and series resistance 
is the most important two of factors limiting the performance of perovskite solar cell. Shunt resistance and 
surface recombination plays slight roles in PCE when they are greater than 104Ω • cm2 and less than 104cm/s, 
respectively. Auger recombination has almost no impact on the device performance.   
