                    The electron transport layer (ETL) is a key component of regular perovskite solar cells to promote the overall charge extraction efficiency and tune the crystallinity of the perovskite layer for better device performance. The authors present a novel protocol of ETL engineering by incorporating a composition of the perovskite precursor, methylammonium chloride (MACl), or formamidine chloride (FACl), into SnO
                    <jats:sub>2</jats:sub>
                    layers, which are then converted into the crystal nuclei of perovskites by reaction with PbI
                    <jats:sub>2</jats:sub>
                    . The SnO
                    <jats:sub>2</jats:sub>
