A B S T R A C T
In this study, we synthesize lead carbanion complex to act as interface passivator for inverted perovskite solar 
cells. The strong Pb–C−bond between carbanion and lead-rich perovskite surface can stabilize the underlying 
perovskite to reduce defects and hence enhance photovoltaic performance. The carrier transfer behavior as a 
function of the lead carbanion complex was measured to optimize device performance by surface passivation. 
The devices achieved a power conversion efficiency of 25.16 % with a high open-circuit voltage of 1.17 V and a 
minimal voltage loss of 0.38 V. The perovskite solar cells with carbanion passivation maintained high perfor­
mance over 600 h and had a lifespan in air exceeding 90 days without encapsulation.",Chemical Engineering Journal,Elsevier BV,True,Experimental passivation optimization of single-junction PSCs,False
