10.1038/s41467-025-58111-y,Modulating competitive adsorption of hybrid self-assembled molecules for efficient wide-bandgap perovskite solar cells and tandems,"The employment of self-assembled molecular hybrid could improve buried interface in perovskite solar cells (PSCs). However, the interplay among hybrid self-assembled monolayers (SAMs) during the deposition process has not been well-studied. Herein, we study the interaction between co-adsorbents and commonly used SAM material, [4-(3,6-dimethyl-9H-carbazol-9-yl)butyl]phosphonic acid (Me-4PACz) for wide-bandgap (WBG) PSCs. It is found that the co-adsorbent, 6-aminohexane-1-sulfonic acid (SA) tends to fill the uncovered sites without interference with Me-4PACz, ensuring the formation of a dense hole selective layer. Moreover, the use of SA/Me-4PACz mixed SAMs could effectively reduce the interfacial non-radiative recombination loss, optimize the energy alignment at the buried interface and regulate the crystallization of WBG perovskite. As a result, the 1.77 eV WBG PSCs deliver a power conversion efficiency (PCE) of 20.67% (20.21% certified) and an impressive open-circuit voltage (VOC) of 1.332 V (1.313 V certified). By combining with a 1.26 eV narrow-bandgap (NBG) PSC, we further fabricate 2-terminal all-perovskite tandem solar cells (TSCs) with a PCE of 28.94% (28.78% certified) for 0.087 cm2 and 23.92% for mini-module with an aperture area of 11.3 cm2. The interplay among hybrid self-assembled monolayers (SAMs) during deposition has not been well studied. Here, authors mix co-adsorbents with carbazole-based SAM material to improve the buried interface, achieving efficiency of 20.67% for wide-bandgap solar cells and 28.94% for all-perovskite tandem devices.",Nature Communications,Nature Portfolio,True,Optimizes single-junction wide-bandgap PSCs experimentally,False
10.1016/j.solener.2021.06.060,Incorporating EA+ into PbI2 film for stable multiple cations perovskite solar cells with negligible hysteresis,"Abstract A simple strategy to incorporate ethyl ammonium cations (EA+) into perovskite film using the two-step method showed a direct relationship between cation-ratio and emission wavelength. EA+ could effectively diffuse into lead iodide (PbI2) seed film and drastically enhances perovskite crystallization and photoluminescence quantum yield as well as photo-stability, thermal stability, and humidity stability simultaneously, due to the significant reduction of density of defect states. The newly designed devices are highly preserved and displayed better film surface morphology. In addition, it showed a PCE about 21.32% of the reverse scan and a corresponding PCE of 21.09% from the forward scan with negligible hysteresis. The PCE of EA+-doped perovskite solar cells (PSCs) were nearly unchanged even after 25 days, which reflects an improved stability of perovskite film. The EA+ incorporating technique implements a new path for high-performance and reliable perovskite solar cells.",Solar Energy,Elsevier BV,True,Experimental EA+ doping improves single-junction PSCs,False
