A B S T R A C T
Organic-inorganic hybrid perovskite crystals with a preferred crystal orientation typically exhibit superior crystal 
quality and enhanced device performance. However, controlling the crystal growth and orientation of perov­
skites remains a significant challenge, especially for the vapor-deposited perovskite thin films. In this study, we 
developed a two-dimensional surface induce (2DSI) strategy applied to the PbI2 precursor film and utilized a 
vapor-solid reaction to direct the growth of perovskite thin films with a preferred (001) crystal facet orientation. 
Moreover, this strategy promoted grain growth, increasing the average grain size from 600 nm to 1600 nm. 
Further validation demonstrates that this 2DSI approach is universally applicable to various RP-type 2D 
perovskite phases, including those with PEA, BA, and halide ion substitutions. Devices fabricated using this 
strategy in a p-i-n configuration achieved a power conversion efficiency of 21.38 %. Additionally, the enhanced 
crystal quality enables the device to retain 95 % of its initial efficiency for up to 1568 h without encapsulation. 
This work provides a theoretical foundation and technical route for vapor-phase c",Chemical Engineering Journal,Elsevier BV,True,Experimental film growth and device performance demonstrated,False
