The quality of the interface between the nickel oxide (NiOx) and the perovskite contact is essential to the effi­
ciency and stability of the device. How to effectively suppress the reaction at the interface between NiOx and 
perovskite is the key to improve the interface quality. Herein, a simple and scalable interface enhancement 
strategy for building efficient and stable perovskite solar cells (PSCs) using 4-aminobenzoic acid (ABA) molecules 
to modify the sputtered NiOx surface as the hole transport layers (HTLs). Meanwhile, ABA molecules not only 
