Printable mesoscopic perovskite solar cells (PM-PSCs) possess notable merits in terms of cost-
effectiveness, easy manufacturing, and large scale applications. Nevertheless, the absence of a hole trans-
port layer contributes to the exacerbation of carrier recombination, and the defects between the per-
ovskite and electron transport layer (ETL) interfaces signiﬁcantly decrease the efﬁciency of the devices.
In this study, a bifunctional surface passivation approach is proposed by applying a thioacetamide
