A B S T R A C T
The industrialization of low-cost printable mesoscopic perovskite solar cells (p-MPSCs) awaits the advancement 
of power conversion efficiency (PCE), which is restricted by defect-assisted non-radiative recombination. Here, 
we report the alkyl chain length engineering of the zwitterionic sulfobetaine passivator to suppress non-radiative 
recombination for preparing high-efficiency p-MPSCs. Increasing the alkyl length decentralizes the positive 
charge of the quaternary ammonium in the sulfobetaine due to the induced effect, and thus weakens the internal 
interaction between the positive ammonium group and the negative sulfonic group. The reduced internal 
interaction fortifies the interaction between the sulfonic group and the perovskite, and brings about well 
enhanced defect passivation, which improves the carrier lifetime of more than 5 folds. On the other hand, 
lengthy alkyl chain tends to induce aggregation between adjacent sulfobetaine molecules, and thus impairs the 
device fill factor which restricts further performance enhancement. The tailored sulfobetaine passivator with the 
octyl group possessing an optimal chain length successfully improves the PCE of p-MPSCs",Chemical Engineering Journal,Elsevier BV,True,Experimental passivation optimization for single-junction PSCs,False
