The optimization of the performance of carbon electrodes to boost hole extraction and suppress charge recom­
bination is a direct and effective approach to achieve high-performance carbon-based perovskite solar cells (C- 
PSCs) without hole transport materials (HTMs). Here, the N-doped carbon nanospheres (NC) compounded in situ 
with WS2 and Pt metal (WS2-Pt/NC) are developed as carbon electrodes for HTM-free C-PSCs. Arising from the 
comprehensive actions of the p-type behavior of WS2, the high conductivity of Pt, and the doping effect of N 
elements, the resulting WS2-Pt/NC electrodes exhibit excellent hole mobility and conductivity with an increased 
work function, which enhance hole extraction and decrease the energy barrier at the back interface of C-PSCs. 
The electron-rich N and S elements in WS2-Pt/NC show a healing effect on the surface cationic defects of the 
perovskite layer, especially the formation of Pb-S bonds between perovskite and WS2 establishes a bridge for 
efficient hole transport, which decrease the monomolecular recombination and increase hole transfer. Finally, 
