ABSTRACT
Inorganic perovskite cesium lead bromide (CsPbBr3) gets extensive attention
due to its superb stability and moisture-tolerance feature. Here, solution-pro-
cessed CsPbBr3 perovskite ﬁlms and their based solar cells were fabricated in
ambient condition. The effect of post-annealing on the properties of the CsPbBr3
ﬁlm grown and the photoelectric performance of perovskite solar cells (PSCs)
have been systematically investigated, which enhances the device power con-
version efﬁciency (PCE) from 2.67 to 5.20%. Moreover, by doping mesoporous
TiO2 (m-TiO2) with reduced graphene oxide (RGO), the PCE of solar cells
attained an apparent enhancement and ﬁnally improved to 7.08%. Not only
high-quality CsPbBr3 perovskite ﬁlms but also high-performance mesoporous
PSCs were obtained by ﬁlm post-annealing and electron transport layer (ETL)
doping, which were all fabricated in ambient conditions.
