Polarity and acidebase equilibrium of the A-site ions in organic-inorganic hybrid perovskites are the
major origins of structure instability that limits the efﬁciency of perovskite solar cells (PSCs). It is effective
to stabilize the structure of perovskite by partial replacement of A-site ions with larger radius and non-
polar ions. Here, we fabricate tetramethylammonium ions N(CH3)4þ (TMAþ) substituting perovskite, MA1-
xTMAxPbI3, by partially replacing MAþ in MAPbI3 with large and rigid TMAþ. Theoretical and experi-
mental study demonstrates that the introduction of TMAþ cation in MA1-xTMAxPbI3 perovskite leads to a
more stable crystal structure and reduces the defects state density in perovskite ﬁlms. The PSCs based on
MA1-xTMAxPbI3 (x ¼ 0.15) ﬁlms demonstrate a champion efﬁciency of 22.23% and an improved stability
against air environment. This work highlights the signiﬁcance of A-site ionic characteristics of perovskite
structure and provides a new strategy in constructing high efﬁciency and stable hybrid PSCs.
