All-brominated inorganic perovskite CsPbBr3 has received much attention in the ﬁeld of optoelectronic
applications owing to its superb stability and ease of manufacture under the ambient condition. How-
ever, the tedious process and toxic solvent are two major challenges for fabrication of CsPbBr3 ﬁlms via a
multi-step deposition method. Here, we demonstrate a sustainable bi-solvent system for preparing high-
quality CsPbBr3 ﬁlms in a triple-step solution-processed route, where the bi-solvent system comprises of
green solvent water and ethylene glycol monomethyl ether (EGME) in place of the noxious methanol for
