Morphology and crystallization control are critical for metal halide perovskite ﬁlms in enabling high-
performance photovoltaic devices. However, they remain particularly challenging for sprayed devices
due to the inherent ﬂaw of the spraying technologydthe “coffee-ring” effect (CRE). Herein, we report a
moisture-assisted strategy that effectively eliminates CRE and enhances ﬁlm crystallization through the
combined utilization of humidity control and water additives. This approach leads to the formation of
Cs0.19FA0.81PbI2.5Br0.5 perovskite ﬁlms with homogeneous morphology and excellent crystallization, and
the power conversion efﬁciency (PCE) of the champion perovskite solar cells increases from 18.25% to
