stability as well as reproducibility of the inverted perovskite solar cells (PSCs). Herein, an efficient interface 
modification strategy based on cinnamyl alcohol (CA) has been proposed to solve these challenges. As a result, 
the wettability of the perovskite on the surface of the PTAA film is significantly improved, which correspondingly 
enhances the film quality of the perovskite layer and the interface contact with the PTAA layer. At the same time, 
the trap states as well as interface energy loss are greatly eliminated, and promotes the improvement of device 
performance, stability and reproducibility. The short-circuited and abnormal devices have been eliminated, and 
repeatability of devices are dramatically improved with CA treatment. The average power conversion efficiency 
