An effective way to prepare efficient and stable organic electronic transport layer (ETL) to solve the problems 
such as interface charge recombination, electrons extraction and transport, and poor interface contact of 
perovskite solar cells (PSCs). Here, a small molecule, AQX-OCH2CF3, termed AQF, is designed, synthesized, and 
incorporated into [6,6]-Phenyl C61-butyric acid methyl ester (PCBM) as ETL for the fabrication of inverted PSCs. 
Multiple experimental tests confirm that AQF can effectively inhibit the charge recombination, optimize the 
