Inorganic cesium lead triiodide perovskite (CsPbI3) exhibits remarkable potential in photovoltaic
applications due to its exemplary thermal stability. However, CsPbI3 is extremely sensitive to moisture
which hinders its practical application in stable and high-eﬃciency photovoltaic devices. Here we show
an eﬀective method to enhance water resistance of CsPbI3 via an ultrathin hydrophobic lead silicate
(PbSiO3) glass layer. The resulting CsPbI3 inorganic perovskite solar cells achieved a remarkably eﬃciency
of 20.59% under standard test conditions. More importantly, the unencapsulated devices possess
outstanding moisture resilience and maintain about 92% of their initial eﬃciency even after being stored
at 25 ± 5% relative humidity (RH) for 600 hours.
