Hydrazine derivatives have been extensively studied as some of the earliest reductants for Sn–Pb mixed
perovskite precursors. However, phenyl hydrazine (BH) as a strong reductant for Sn-based perovskite
solutions has not been reported yet, and Sn2+ is unusually oxidized in the precursor solution with BH
additives in our experiment. Thus, not all organic reductants are suitable as additives, and therefore
selecting a suitable reductant should be paid special attention to. Herein, it is found that BH as a
Brønsted base deprotonates MA+ to produce HI, which further catalyzes the oxidation of Sn2+ by DMSO.
As an alternative, hydrochloride phenyl hydrazine with a sulfonic amide group (–SO2–NH2) is added to
the precursor as a reductant and passivator. As a result, a power conversion efficiency of 22.01% is
achieved, and prolonged shelf stability is realized.
