A B S T R A C T
The interfacial energy level mismatch between the functional layers of perovskite solar cells (PSCs), especially
between the perovskite layer (PVK) and the hole transport layer (HTL), is a major issue restricting the
enhancement of performance of PSCs. In this study, [6,6]-phenyl C61-butyric acid methyl ester (PCBM), a
fullerene derivative, is introduced to modulate the energy level array in the interface of PVK/HTL. It is
demonstrated that the modification by n-type material PCBM can effectively decrease the energy level difference
between perovskite and spiro-OMeTAD, and enhance the Fermi level of perovskite to form a band bending
energy level structure, which accelerate the extraction of holes and improve the electrical property of perovskite
film.",Chemical Engineering Journal,Elsevier BV,True,Experimental interface optimization of single-junction PSCs,False
