fluoroethylamine hydrochloride (F3EACl) with permanent dipole moment is devised to modify the perovskite 
interface. Highly electronegative trifluoro groups can accelerate the dielectric response of perovskite films, 
intensify the dielectric screening effect, and significantly suppress non-radiative recombination of charge car­
riers. Meanwhile, the –NH3
+ group in F3EACl effectively passivates the defects at the perovskite surface, further 
