The topochemical assembly along coherent interfaces governs the growth of
polycrystalline perovskite ﬁlms and facilitates orientation manipulation. By
exploring alternative assembly pathways, we successfully obtain an optimal (001)-
oriented ﬁlm with minimized lattice heterogeneity and electronic disorder. The
inverted solar cells achieve a T80 lifetime of 6,418 h during light-heat aging,
retaining over 99% of the initial power conversion efﬁciency after 2,500 h at the
maximum power point tracking under one-sun illumination.
