transport layer (ETL). This study introduces a novel composite ETL, synthesized via a hydrothermal method, 
incorporating polypyrrole (PPy) and copper (Cu) into molybdenum diselenide (MoSe2). The PPy@CuMoSe2 
composite exhibited improved crystallinity, optimized surface morphology, and a reduced bandgap, which 
enhanced charge transport and minimized recombination losses. PSCs using PPy@CuMoSe2 achieved a short 
circuit current density (Jsc) of 16.5 mA/cm2, an open circuit voltage (Voc) of 0.96 V, and a fill factor of 94 %, 
yielding a power conversion efficiency (PCE) of 14.89 % a 75.8 % improvement over pristine MoSe2 (PCE = 8.47 
%). The superior performance stems from the synergistic effect of PPy and Cu, which enhance interfacial charge 
transport and minimize recombination. This work highlights the potential of rationally designed composites to 
