10.1021/acsaem.1c01568,Strategy for Crystallization Management of Perovskite: Incorporation of FAI in a PbI<sub>2</sub> Precursor for a Two-Step Spin-Coating Process,"FAMACs triple-cation perovskite is an excellent organic–inorganic perovskite material widely used in solar cells, light-emitting diodes (LEDs), and other optoelectronic devices. This work proposes a crystallization management strategy by adding formamidinium iodide (FAI) to PbI 2 precursor in a two-step spin-coating process for FAMACs perovskite solar cells and obtains the best PCE of 22.88%. Nonstoichiometric FAI interacts with PbI 2 to form FAI-PbI 2 low-dimensional perovskites, which is demonstrated using X-ray diffraction (XRD), UV–vis, and X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS) measurements. The efficiency and stability of the cells are improved due to the improvement in the perovskite crystal quality and reduced crystal defects.",ACS Applied Energy Materials,American Chemical Society,True,Experimental optimization of perovskite crystallization for single-junction PSC,False
