A B S T R A C T  
Charge transport facilitation in the electron transport layer is necessary for high-efficiency perovskite solar cells. 
Carbonaceous materials such as graphene (G) and carbon nanotubes (CNTs) have been extensively used in energy 
storage and conversion applications. Here we report the novel design of ETL based on the combinations of tin 
oxide, graphene nanoribbons, nitrogen-doped graphene nanoribbons, and gold nanoparticles for 2D/3D perov­
skite solar cells. Three different ETLs were employed to get three 2D/3D PSCs with novel device architectures. 
The effect of different ETLs on the performance of solar cells is investigated. Results reveal that due to better 
optical and electrical behavior, the solar cell employing a composite of tin oxide, graphene nanoribbons, 
nitrogen-doped graphene nanoribbons, and gold nanoparticles as ETL has attained a higher PCE of 10.77%.   
