10.1016/j.joule.2024.01.021,Utilizing electrostatic dynamic bonds in zwitterion elastomer for self-curing of flexible perovskite solar cells,"Article
Utilizing electrostatic dynamic bonds in
zwitterion elastomer for self-curing of ﬂexible
perovskite solar cells
The performance of f-PSCs has been limited by the intrinsic rigidity of perovskite
materials and uncontrollable crystallization of perovskite thin ﬁlms on ﬂexible
substrates. In this work, the zwitterion elastomer has been introduced to regulate
the perovskite nucleation and crystal growth steps, engendering reﬁned ﬁlm
morphology. The zwitterion fusion under mild stimuli also triggers an instant self-
curing ability for the cracked ﬂexible ﬁlms, endowing the f-PSCs with impressive
mechanical durability and a record PCE of 24.51% (certiﬁed 24.04%).
