Lee and co-workers report adverse effects at FAPbI3/SnO2x (SnO2 with oxygen
vacancies) from a crystallographic aspect. The absence of oxygen atoms at the
interface induces formation of iodine interstitials that initiate a-FAPbI3
degradation. Also, the absence of oxygen atoms loosely bound organic cations in
the lattice, which led to poor operational stability of perovskite solar cells.
Oxidized black phosphorus quantum dots were employed to thoroughly passivate
oxygen vacancies in SnO2x, and the best power conversion efﬁciency of 23.23%
was achieved with superior operational stability.
