10.1016/j.joule.2023.05.020,Solvent racing crystallization: Low-solvation dispersion cosolvents for high-quality halide perovskites in photovoltaics,"Article
Solvent racing crystallization: Low-solvation
dispersion cosolvents for high-quality halide
perovskites in photovoltaics
We present an innovative method that leverages the combined effects of solvent
polarity and hydrogen-bonding property to tailor the solvation capacity of ACN-
DME (i.e., acetonitrile and 1,2-dimethoxyethane) dispersion cosolvents. This
strategy enables enhanced solubility of perovskite precursors and facilitates the
rapid crystallization of well-deﬁned intermediate ﬁlms. The resulting perovskite
ﬁlms exhibited exceptional crystallinity and preferred orientation, which are crucial
for achieving high-performance perovskite solar modules.
